{"shard": 16, "documents": [{"id": "1872", "title": "2026 APPROPRIATION ACT Details pdf", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2026-appropriation-act-details", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2026-appropriation-act-details", "text": "2026 APPROPRIATION ACT Details pdf \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center\">News\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail 2026 APPROPRIATION ACT Details Home 2026 APPROPRIATION ACT Details 2026 APPROPRIATION ACT Details pdf Published on 10 August 2026 File Name: 2026 APPROPRIATION ACT Details_pdf.pdf File Size: 77.06 MB File Type: application/pdf Hits: 1950 Hits Created Date: 08-10-2026 Download View Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "3d5a81b198c785c2d8e5045c7caa342ce1794351516ecf16f759a65be73b543f", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:20.697591+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1873", "title": "Meet The Newly Appointed Director General Of SON, Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2023/10/19/1643/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2023/10/19/1643/", "text": "Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke\u2019s professional journey includes vital roles in public and private institutions, where he has excelled as a Tax Executive, Financial Consultant, and Tax Manager. Notably, he served as the Interim Chairman and Chief Executive Officer of the Imo State Internal Revenue Service, leading a team that significantly increased internally generated revenue from 700 million naira to over 2 billion naira monthly. He has also served as a branch Business Head in a top International Financial Institution with a background operating as a Top Management Officer in public and private Institutions. Throughout his career, He has demonstrated exceptional skills in leadership, negotiation, budgeting, and credit analysis. As the Director General, he will be responsible for running the organization\u2019s day-to-day administration empowered by the Council\u2019s directives. His responsibilities extend to advising the Council in formulating, implementing, and reviewing national policies on standardization, quality control, and metrology. He will be crucial in coordinating the activities of Directors, initiating investigations, and representing the Organization at national and international levels. His appointment as Director General brings a seasoned professional with a track record of transformative leadership. His commitment to excellence, financial acumen, and strategic vision make him a valuable addition to SON as we strive for excellence in our mission and objectives.", "content_hash": "e16e45f27408211e2d9afad71c364ca52d0ac4379752705e21a991a3d94f2367", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:22.599646+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1874", "title": "2026 Appropriation Bill FINAL", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2026-appropriation-bill-final", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2026-appropriation-bill-final", "text": "2026 Appropriation Bill FINAL \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center\">News\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail 2026 Appropriation Bill FINAL Home 2026 Appropriation Bill FINAL 2026 Appropriation Bill FINAL Published on 10 August 2026 File Name: file_6a7a2d3c21e9c_2026 Appropriation Bill FINAL.pdf File Size: 261.34 KB File Type: application/pdf Hits: 840 Hits Created Date: 08-10-2026 Download View Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "d576052cf3f7af47dd13cbc55c475f435d62064e165d71701caf5de216f98594", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:23.802190+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1875", "title": "SON MSC Department Secures IAS Accreditation For Four (4) Management System Standards", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/02/28/son-msc-department-secures-ias-accreditation-for-four-4-management-system-standards/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/02/28/son-msc-department-secures-ias-accreditation-for-four-4-management-system-standards/", "text": "The Standards Organisation of Nigeria\u2019s (SON) Management Systems Certification (MSC) department has been granted accreditation by the International Accreditation Service (IAS) for four globally recognized Management System Standards. The AUTHORITY reports that the feat is said to be a testament to the dedication to quality and best practices put in place in SON MSC. A statement issued by the organisation listed the four Management System Standards as follows: Quality Management System (QMS) ISO 9001:2015, Occupational Health and Safety Management System (OHSMS) ISO 45001:2018, Environmental Management System (EMS) ISO 14001:2015 and Food Safety Management System (FSMS) ISO 22000:2018. The remarkable accomplishment follows a rigorous assessment process conducted by IAS, verifying that the SON MSC department\u2019s operations and audits conducted by SON auditors, comprehensively meet the stringent requirements of these international standards. The accreditation signifies the department\u2019s unwavering commitment to delivering exceptional quality in all its services, upholding the highest standards in occupational health and safety, and minimizing environmental impact through responsible practices. Others are ensuring food safety and quality across the supply chain and adhering to industry-leading benchmarks in the aerospace, defense, and transportation sectors. Expressing delight over the development, Engr Obiageli P. Egbuciem, Acting Director, SON MSC department declared that the accreditation is a badge of honor for the SON MSC department and a global recognition to the organisation. She further stated that \u201cthis accreditation not only recognizes the efforts of the SON MSC department but also underscores the proficiency and expertise of SON auditors, whose meticulous evaluations played a significant role in achieving this milestone. \u201cTheir dedication to upholding industry standards and conducting thorough audits has been instrumental in ensuring the department\u2019s adherence to best practices.\u201d In conclusion, she stated \u201cIt\u2019s a direct reflection of our team\u2019s relentless pursuit of excellence and unwavering commitment to international best practices. We are incredibly proud of this achievement, and it serves as a catalyst for further advancements in our journey towards continuous improvement.\u201d", "content_hash": "90fd9697e3941a9bdcfdbd3356a12e49be5df51c77b45722dee520cae82172c6", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:25.944424+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1876", "title": "2025 Appropriation Bill", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2025-appropriation-bill", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2025-appropriation-bill", "text": "2025 Appropriation Bill \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center\">News\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail 2025 Appropriation Bill Home 2025 Appropriation Bill 2025 Appropriation Bill Published on 18 December 2024 File Name: 2025 Draft Bill.pdf File Size: 318.68 KB File Type: application/pdf Hits: 31600 Hits Created Date: 12-18-2024 Download View Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "dab24b777a8ec8dd24fb73703a44798d16485a6670ef3ebe1aa230b8c592364f", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:26.269439+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1877", "title": "British American Tobacco (BAT) Pays Courtesy Visit to Standards Organisation Of Nigeria", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/02/28/british-american-tobacco-bat-pays-courtesy-visit-to-standards-organisation-of-nigeria/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/02/28/british-american-tobacco-bat-pays-courtesy-visit-to-standards-organisation-of-nigeria/", "text": "In a concerted effort to bolster industry standards and contribute to Nigeria\u2019s economic diversification drive, British American Tobacco (BAT) recently paid a courtesy visit to the Standards Organisation of Nigeria\u2019s (SON) Operational Headquarters in Lekki, Lagos. The team, in consonance with the Federal Government\u2019s initiative to facilitate ease of doing business and support industries as partners in progress, was warmly received by Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke, the Director General of SON. Dr. Okeke emphasized SON\u2019s readiness to collaborate with stakeholders keen on advancing the country\u2019s interests through job creation and revenue generation from imports and exports. This move seeks to pivot the nation\u2019s focus from petroleum products to its other abundant resources. Dr. Ifeanyi Okeke (DG, SON), presenting a plaque to Mr. Yarub Al-Bahranij (MD, BAT) Expressing gratitude for the reception, Mr. Yarub Al-Bahranij, the Managing Director of BAT, assured those present of the company\u2019s unwavering commitment to maintaining standards, self-regulating its processes, and staying abreast of the industry\u2019s evolving trends. Dr. Okeke reiterated SON\u2019s role as a regulatory body and guardian of standards, highlighting the importance of soliciting feedback from industry players and stakeholders. He noted that for new products such as vaping devices, heated tobacco products, and electronic tobacco heating devices, a comprehensive approach would be taken to ensure outcomes beneficial to all parties involved. This strategic move aims not only to create more job opportunities but also to enhance the nation\u2019s economy. In his closing remarks, Mr. Yarub pledged BAT\u2019s continuous cooperation and collaboration with SON, particularly in areas of sensitization, corporate responsibility, and enforcement. As partners in progress, BAT affirmed its commitment to upholding ethical practices, even when under minimal scrutiny. The meeting witnessed the presence of key management members, including Mr. Uchenna Okafor, Chief of Staff to the DG, Mr. Yunusa Mohammed Bala, Head of the Food Codex Group, Mrs. Odiri Erewa-Meggison, External Affairs Director, Mr. Pat Rich, Legal Director, and Mrs. Ruth Owojaiye, Head of Regulatory Engagements. This gathering marks a significant step towards fostering a mutually beneficial relationship between BAT and SON, aimed at ensuring industry excellence and economic growth in Nigeria.", "content_hash": "037b11585d5007feb4d831dd513ec9b4af47a67b8a97839f1c63797e676fca65", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:28.555409+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1878", "title": "2025 Executive Proposal", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2025-executive-proposal", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/2025-executive-proposal", "text": "2025 Executive Proposal \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center\">News\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail 2025 Executive Proposal Home 2025 Executive Proposal 2025 Executive Proposal Published on 18 December 2024 File Name: 2025 ExecutiveProposal_Final.pdf File Size: 6.22 MB File Type: application/pdf Hits: 12467 Hits Created Date: 12-18-2024 Download View Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "9dfc6f70b8e14026a773b12d583f4c5c3f522c694d4799a057ef9bd0b5ad2a16", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:29.240552+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1879", "title": "BSI Shares Vision for SON\u2019s Role in Achieving National Quality Policy Objectives", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/03/14/bsi-shares-vision-for-sons-role-in-achieving-national-quality-policy-objectives/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/03/14/bsi-shares-vision-for-sons-role-in-achieving-national-quality-policy-objectives/", "text": "In a bid to bolster Nigeria\u2019s National Quality Infrastructure (NQI), the British Standards Institute (BSI), recognized as the National Standards Body of the United Kingdom, is gearing up for a strategic partnership with the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON). This collaboration aims to align with the overarching objectives of the National Quality Policy (NQP) and the Nigeria National Standardization Strategy (NNSS). A high-level delegation from BSI, led by Mr. James Richardson, recently paid a visit to SON\u2019s corporate headquarters in Abuja, laying the groundwork for this transformative initiative. The delegation held extensive discussions with SON\u2019s Director-General and CEO, Dr. Ifeanyi Chinonso Okeke, outlining a comprehensive plan to support SON in its efforts towards achieving the NQP objectives. During the meeting, BSI emphasized crucial components of their action plan, focusing on key steps to bolster SON\u2019s capacity and drive the NQI forward. One of these steps is Training Initiatives which is about recognizing the pivotal role of standards development. BSI stressed the importance of training SON\u2019s technical secretaries, committee members, and group heads. A comprehensive training session is slated to commence on April 1st, 2024 and this aims to equip SON\u2019s team with the requisite skills needed to spearhead the NQI. Another step is to promote the sales of Standards. The significance of SON\u2019s marketing department in promoting the adoption and sales of standards within Nigeria was highlighted. This strategic approach not only enhances awareness but also serves as a revenue-generating avenue for the organization. The BSI delegation also emphasized that Public Awareness and Collaboration is a necessity for active engagement with key stakeholders through robust sensitization and collaboration activities. SON\u2019s Public Relations Department will be pivotal in fostering partnerships and disseminating information about the NQI\u2019s objectives and benefits. Impressed by the detailed action plan presented by the BSI delegation, Dr. Okeke commended their dedication to the project and the progress achieved thus far. He underscored the critical role SON plays in advancing Nigeria\u2019s quality infrastructure and reaffirmed the organization\u2019s commitment to realizing the objectives of the NQP. The collaborative efforts between BSI and SON mark a significant stride toward establishing a robust National Quality Infrastructure in Nigeria. With a shared vision of excellence and adherence to international standards, this partnership holds the promise of driving innovation, enhancing market competitiveness, and ensuring the highest standards of quality for Nigerian products and services on the global stage.", "content_hash": "ac612a6b0790a21a2bbbc527ab49175af25972520b1f4796b031c3db727f5733", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:31.228894+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1880", "title": "National Public Sector Solarisation Initiative Launched: A Bold Step Towards Sustainable Energy and Economic Growth.", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/media-center/news/national-public-sector-solarisation-initiative-launched-a-bold-step-towards-sustainable-energy-and-economic-growth", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/media-center/news/national-public-sector-solarisation-initiative-launched-a-bold-step-towards-sustainable-energy-and-economic-growth", "text": "National Public Sector Solarisation Initiative Launched: A Bold Step Towards Sustainable Energy and Economic Growth. In a landmark move aimed at transforming Nigeria\u2019s energy infrastructure and driving economic development, the Director-General of the Budget Office of the Federation, Mr. Tanimu Yakubu, today signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) with key government agencies to kickstart the National Public Sector Solarisation Initiative (NPSSI). The signing ceremony, held at the Budget Office headquarters in Abuja, marked a significant milestone in the country\u2019s quest for sustainable energy solutions and innovative financing models. The MOU was signed in collaboration with the Rural Electrification Agency (REA), the Ministry of Finance Incorporated (MOFI), and the Infrastructure Corporation of Nigeria (InfraCorp). The initiative seeks to deploy solar energy infrastructure across the nation, targeting 75.5 million Nigerians, while fostering local manufacturing, job creation, and skills development. In his remarks, Mr. Tanimu Yakubu highlighted the importance of the NPSSI as a strategic partnership to bridge the energy gap and stimulate economic growth. \u201cThis initiative is a proof to our renewed commitment to leveraging innovative financing and sustainable solutions to address critical infrastructure challenges. By working with REA and MOFI, we aim to catalyze funding, build local competencies, and create a ripple effect across the economy,\u201d he stated. The Managing Director of the Rural Electrification Agency, Dr. Abba Abubakar Aliyu, emphasized the transformative potential of the initiative. \u201cThe NPSSI is not just about providing electricity; it\u2019s about energizing education, empowering communities, and creating a sustainable future. By localizing supply chains and building local capabilities, we are planting the seeds for long-term growth and development,\u201d he said. Representing the Ministry of Finance Incorporated, Dr. Femi Ogunseinde, Executive Director of Investments, echoed these sentiments, stressing the need for fiscal sustainability and scalable projects. \u201cThis initiative is a blueprint for how public-private partnerships can drive large-scale impact. By focusing on local manufacturing and innovative funding models, we are laying the foundation for a resilient and self-sufficient economy,\u201d he noted. Dr. Lazarus Angbazo, Managing Director of the Infrastructure Corporation, also underscored the importance of the initiative in addressing critical infrastructure gaps. \u201cThe NPSSI is a bold step towards achieving energy security and economic prosperity. By leveraging local competencies and scalable solutions, we are setting the stage for a brighter future for all Nigerians,\u201d he said. The MOU was signed by the key stakeholders, including legal representation from Hajia Maryam Saleh Hassan of the Budget Office, marking a historic collaboration for Nigeria's energy future. The signing ceremony was attended by key directors from the Budget Office of the Federation, including Mrs. Modupeola Lasekan (Economic Expenditure), Mr. Muhammad Yusuf (Social Expenditure), Mr. Gajo Baidi (Budget Monitoring & Evaluation), Mrs. Nonye Onyekwu (Revenue & Fiscal Policy), and Mr. Isyaku Sani (Human Resource). The NPSSI represents a groundbreaking effort to address Nigeria\u2019s energy challenges while fostering economic growth, job creation, and sustainable development. With its focus on local manufacturing, innovative financing, and scalable solutions, the initiative is poised to transform the nation\u2019s energy infrastructure and unlock new opportunities for millions of Nigerians. As the country embarks on this ambitious journey, the NPSSI stands as a shining example of how collaboration, innovation, and strategic planning can drive meaningful change and pave the way for a brighter future. Dr. Afolabi Olajuwon, fniprHead, Information & Public Relations For media inquiries, please contact:Budget Office of the Federation Email: This email address is being protected from spambots. You need JavaScript enabled to view it. Phone: \u202a+234 800 123 4567 Share", "content_hash": "a4d59a2888abbbf3b1eb72d5df5275767df77182fcd6376fe8e20c04e40edd26", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:32.042306+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1881", "title": "SON Presents 80 Newly Approved Standards on CNG Road Vehicle and Related Appliances to the Presidential Compressed National Gas Initiative", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/03/14/son-presents-80-newly-approved-standards-on-cng-road-vehicle-and-related-appliances-to-the-presidential-compressed-national-gas-initiative/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/03/14/son-presents-80-newly-approved-standards-on-cng-road-vehicle-and-related-appliances-to-the-presidential-compressed-national-gas-initiative/", "text": "In its efforts to promote safety and quality in the energy sector, the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) presented 80 newly approved Nigerian Industrial Standards for Compressed Natural Gas Road Vehicles and Related Appliances to the Presidential Compressed Natural Gas Initiative (PCNGI) in the SON Corporate Headquarters in Abuja yesterday. The Director General/ Chief Executive of SON, Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke presented eighty (80) Standards and Guidelines for Compressed Natural Gas Road Vehicle and related appliances approved by the Honorable Minister, Industry, Trade and Investment, Dr. Doris Nkiruka Uzoka \u2013 Anite to the Presidential Compressed Natural Gas Initiative, Led by the Programme Director/Chief Executive, Presidential Compressed Natural Gas Initiative, Engr. Michael Oluwagbemi, the committee received the standards which encompass a wide range of technical specifications and requirements, including CNG Conversion kit, standards for electrical connections and vehicle diagnostics, standards for road-worthiness and Vehicle safety, standards for CNG storage vessels, and standards for CNG refueling stations, as well as guideline for installation of specific components to support the use of compressed natural gas (CNG) for vehicle propulsion. In his remarks, the SON helmsman stated that the presentation of the standards by SON is the beginning of the journey towards safer, more reliable, cheaper, environmentally sustainable, and most importantly alternative fuel utilization across our nation for road vehicles and other CNG-related appliances.\u201d The Director General stressed that SON\u2019s commitment to excellence and innovation in line with international best practices has culminated in the development and approval of these standards, which represent a significant milestone in SON\u2019s efforts to promote safety and quality in the energy sector. Dr. Okeke explained that the Presidential Compressed Natural Gas Initiative is a component of the palliative intervention of President Bola Ahmed Tinubu\u2019s administration and one of the many steps taken by the president to ensure his Renewed Hope Agenda is enjoyed by every Nigerian. He called on all the relevant stakeholders and the public to support the Renewed Hope Agenda of President Bola Ahmed Tinubu for a better and sustainable future for our nation. In presenting an overview of the newly approved Standards, the SON Director, Standards Development, Engr. Yahya Bukar, explained that SON was tasked to develop and deliver these standards within a limited time frame, a challenge the organisation under the guidance of the SON Director General/Chief Executive was able to achieve. He thanked all the industry experts, regulators, academics, and other relevant stakeholders who worked hard with SON to achieve this feat. In his response, the Programme Director, PCNGI, Engr. Michael Oluwagbemi, commended SON for working hard to ensure that the 80 standards were developed and approved speedily. He stated that the effort by SON to develop these standards imbibes the vision of the president to make life better for Nigerians. The Presidential Compressed Natural Gas Initiative committee comprises of relevant regulatory agencies such as the National Mid-Stream Down-stream Petroleum Regulatory Authority (NMDPRA), Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), Nigerian Institute of Transport Technology (NITT), National Automotive Design and Development Council (NADDC), Ministry of Finance Incorporation (MOFI), Federal Road Safety Corps (FRSC) and other key stakeholders.", "content_hash": "a6149c5ed327d8a08562a69572adbe748d4b07e05a362fbd4e072e54bab10539", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:33.859562+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1882", "title": "SON Announces Five(5) Outstanding National Qualifiers of Arso Essay Competition 2023/2024", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/05/09/son-announces-five5-outstanding-national-qualifiers-of-arso-essay-competition-2023-2024/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/05/09/son-announces-five5-outstanding-national-qualifiers-of-arso-essay-competition-2023-2024/", "text": "The Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) has revealed the national qualifiers for the 11th annual essay competition organized by the African Organisation for Standardisation (ARSO). These five outstanding individuals have been selected to represent Nigeria at the continental level: \u2013 Oguejiofor Nkemakonam Anthony, University of Lagos \u2013 Bosede Oyola David, University of Ibadan \u2013 Jimoh Marian, Ahmadu Bello University, Zaria \u2013 Akinola Oluwafemi Semiire, University of Nigeria, Nsukka \u2013 Abdulganiu Abdulwasiu Olanrewaju, Federal University of Health Sciences, Azare The Director General/Chief Executive of SON, Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke, emphasized that the competition is not only about winning but also about instilling the values of standardisation in the youth, who are the future leaders. He urged continual diligence from the assessors and screening committee members, expressing hope that these representatives will be winners at the continental level and make Nigeria proud. Dr. Okeke emphasized the significance of standardisation in ensuring consistency, reliability, and quality assurance in products and services. He highlighted the theme of this year\u2019s competition, \u201cEmpowering Consumers through Standardisation to Achieve their Rights to Safe Quality Goods and Services,\u201d underscoring the pivotal role of standardisation in consumer empowerment and development acceleration. He commended the efforts of the committee members and emphasized the importance of spreading awareness about standardisation\u2019s potential to enhance lives, the economy, and the environment. He stressed the need for collaboration among government, industry, and civil society stakeholders to uphold consumers\u2019 fundamental rights to safe quality goods and services. The Inter-ministerial Screening Committee, comprising members from various government agencies including the Federal Ministry of Education, Federal Ministry of Women Affairs, Consumer Protection Commission, Federal Ministry of Humanitarian Affairs and Poverty Alleviation, FCCPC, National Human Rights Commission, Independent Corrupt Practices Commission (ICPC), and SON as the Secretariat, played a crucial role in the selection process.", "content_hash": "f0831b1788dc9df30810bee7e862da5889027cde6c21527ba98f77e394e505af", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:38.014755+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1883", "title": "2024 Budget Proposal Presentation", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/media-center/news/2024-budget-proposal-presentation", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/media-center/news/2024-budget-proposal-presentation", "text": "2024 Budget Proposal Presentation \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact active\">Media Center current-item active\">News\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail News Home Media Center News 2024 Budget Proposal Presentation News & Events 03 December 2023 2024 Budget Proposal Presentation The Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning team during the 2024 Budget Proposal presentation at the National Assembly. Share Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "5dde5ba2c79bbd3df5411f4f54b33ce6ce5354487a3fcbb77cb191c1cc182f4c", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:38.915564+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1884", "title": "Trade Expo at ARSO 30th General Assembly 2024 to Showcase Nigerian Market", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/05/09/trade-expo-at-arso-30th-general-assembly-2024-to-showcase-nigerian-market/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/05/09/trade-expo-at-arso-30th-general-assembly-2024-to-showcase-nigerian-market/", "text": "As the African Organization for Standardization (ARSO) prepares for its General Assembly scheduled for July in Abuja, anticipation is mounting for a concurrent trade exhibition set to offer a firsthand experience of the vibrant Nigerian market. With an array of local manufacturers and producers slated to participate, the exhibition promises to be a catalyst for economic growth, both for domestic stakeholders and international visitors. The trade exhibition, strategically aligned with the ARSO General Assembly, presents a unique platform for local manufacturers and producers to showcase their products and innovations to a diverse audience of industry experts, policymakers, and potential investors. By highlighting the quality, diversity, and competitiveness of Nigerian goods and services, the exhibition aims to bolster confidence in the country\u2019s market and stimulate both domestic and international trade. For local manufacturers and producers, the benefits of participating in the exhibition are manifold. Firstly, it provides an unparalleled opportunity to network with key stakeholders in the industry, fostering collaborations and partnerships that can drive innovation and growth. Secondly, it offers a chance to gain exposure to international markets, as the General Assembly attracts delegates from across Africa and beyond, opening doors for export opportunities. Additionally, by adhering to ARSO\u2019s standards and regulations, participants can enhance the credibility and marketability of their products, paving the way for sustainable business expansion. On the other hand, visitors to the country attending the ARSO General Assembly will have the privilege of immersing themselves in the dynamic Nigerian market firsthand. From traditional crafts to cutting-edge technologies, the exhibition will showcase the breadth and depth of Nigeria\u2019s economic landscape, providing valuable insights into emerging trends and investment opportunities. Moreover, by engaging directly with local manufacturers and producers, visitors can gain a deeper understanding of Nigeria\u2019s cultural heritage, entrepreneurial spirit, and commitment to excellence. The trade exhibition is poised to enhance the overall experience of the ARSO General Assembly by complementing the discussions and deliberations with tangible demonstrations of economic potential and industrial capability. By showcasing the best of Nigerian innovation and enterprise, the exhibition will underscore the importance of standardization in driving economic development and fostering regional integration. Ultimately, it is hoped that the synergy between the exhibition and the General Assembly will catalyze transformative change, propelling Nigeria and Africa towards a future of sustainable growth and prosperity.", "content_hash": "3cace496f96c557d7ffac7ba1884eca3232c571ee748b2f2dd2b5f30b91ea495", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:40.730437+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1885", "title": "Public Presentation of the 2024 Budget Proposal", "url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/media-center/gallery/view-album/tag-Public%20Presentation%20of%20the%202024%20Budget%20Proposal", "final_url": "https://budgetoffice.gov.ng/index.php/media-center/gallery/view-album/tag-Public%20Presentation%20of%20the%202024%20Budget%20Proposal", "text": "Public Presentation of the 2024 Budget Proposal \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments\">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact active\">Media Center\">News current-item active\">Gallery\">Resources\">Internal Resources\">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports\">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources\">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants Staff mail Mail Gallery Home Media Center Gallery Public Presentation of the 2024 Budget Proposal Budget Office of the FederationThe Budget Office of the Federation was established to provide budget function, and implement budget and fiscal policies of the Federal Government of Nigeria.Quick Links Federal Ministry of Finance Central Bank Of Nigeria Accountant General's Office Open Treasury Data Privacy Policy Office of the Auditor General of the Federation Bureau of Public Service Reform Bureau of Public Procurement Ministry of Budget and Economic Planning NewsletterSignup for our latest news & articles. We won\u2019t give you spam mails. 15398897 Today: 97 Total: 15,398,897 ContactCentral Business Area,P.M.B. 251 Amadu Bello Way Garki,Abuja FCT,Nigeria.info@budgetoffice.gov.ng \u00a9 All Copyright 2022. Budget Office of the Federation - Federal Republic of Nigeria \">Home\">About\">Budget Office of the Federation\">Departments \">Office of the Director General\">Human Resources Management\">Expenditure Social\">Revenue & Fiscal PolicyFinance and Accounts\">Expenditure Economics\">Budget Monitoring and Evaluation\">Management Team\">Contact\">Media Center \">News\">Gallery\">Resources \">Internal Resources \">Budget Documents\">Executive Order\">Policy Documents\">MTEF\">MTSS\">NDP\">OGP\">Publications\">Presentations\">Reports \">Quarterly Budget Implementation\">Fiscal Framework\"> Waivers GrantedCall Circular\">Citizens Guide To The BudgetExternal Resources \">Budget Help Desk\">Citizen's Portal\">Register Participants We use cookies We use cookies on our website. Some of them are essential for the operation of the site, while others help us to improve this site and the user experience (tracking cookies). You can decide for yourself whether you want to allow cookies or not. Please note that if you reject them, you may not be able to use all the functionalities of the site. Ok Decline", "content_hash": "078e5a8297d124c71c01074fb45e4e224f5eabcc3700744de6cb3b77206ea39a", "domain": "budgetoffice.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:40.961815+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1886", "title": "SON, LASG & FTAN Partner to Boost Standardization in the Hospitality Sector", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/05/11/son-lasg-ftan-partner-to-boost-standardization-in-the-hospitality-sector/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/05/11/son-lasg-ftan-partner-to-boost-standardization-in-the-hospitality-sector/", "text": "Director General Dr ifeanyi C. Okeke delivering his opening remarks The Director General, Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), Dr. Ifeanyi C. Okeke, has emphasized the importance of standardization in the Tourism and Hospitality sector. Dr. Okeke made this known at the Conference jointly organized by SON, the Federation of Tourism Association of Nigeria (FTAN) and the Lagos State Government in Lagos recently. In the Conference tagged \u201cImplementing International Best Practices in the Hospitality Business, Dr. Okeke, highlighted the need for SON to collaborate with relevant stakeholders to enforce existing international and national standards, as well as for organisations to demonstrate compliance with global standards in order stay competitive. He emphasized the importance of SON certification processes for the hospitality sector to thrive stating that the NIS ISO 22483:2021: For Hotels services requirements and NIS 489: 2020: hotels and serviced accommodation management system and Rating, requirements and guidance for use if implemented will surely improve on their quality of services provided in the sector. Speaking further the SON Director General, stressed the importance of collaborating with relevant stakeholders to enforce these standards to have a vibrant and sanitized systems thereby adding value to the businesses as well as to promote economic growth for the Tourism and hospitality sector in Nigeria. Equally speaking at the event, Mrs. Oloruntoyin Atekoja, representing Lagos State Ministry of Tourism, harped on the importance of partnership among stakeholders to drive positive change in the hospitality sector and establish new benchmarks for success. She underscored the critical role that standard plays in ensuring quality, consistency, and competitiveness in the tourism sector, serving as the foundation for industry growth within the international community while maintaining the highest service delivery standards. Mrs. Atekoja assured SON\u2019s management of the state\u2019s unwavering commitment and support for initiatives aimed at promoting standardization and excellence in the tourism and hospitality sector. Mr. Nkerewem Onung, President of the Federation of Tourism Associations of Nigeria (FTAN), emphasized the importance of partnership and collaboration to drive positive change in the hospitality sector and establish new benchmarks for success.He applaud SON for the initiative, adding that the private sector is ready to work with Government at all levels. He emphasized on the importance of Tourism, SON needs to appeal to all State Governors on the need to register all hotels in their state as it will benefit both the state and the business owners, noting that until there is a collaborative effort the Standards being targeted will not be attainable.", "content_hash": "27454c1a3ada6380e55d66b62e644a790b2f1321db5ae17f9585fea6b53f31f1", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:42.808473+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1887", "title": "Flow chart for the sales of NIS Standards", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/13/flow-chart-for-the-sales-of-nis-standards/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/13/flow-chart-for-the-sales-of-nis-standards/", "text": "Flow chart for the sales of NIS Standards \u2013 Standards Organisation of Nigeria Skip to main content Hit enter to search or ESC to close Close Search search Menu Home About SON The Organisation Who We Are The Mandate Organogram Meet The Management Team Departments/Units ICT Finance & Accounts HR National Product Certification International Product Certification Inspectorate & Compliance Laboratory Services Legal/Council Marketing Management System Certification National Metrology Institute Corporate Affairs Regi