& Updates Photo Gallery Staff Staff Mail ID Card HRM e-Receipt E-Store e-Service HELP Contact Us Contact SON Branch Locator FAQs SON FAQs PAM FAQ SONCAP FAQ MANCAP FAQ Product Registration FAQ Eder-Services SME Desk Portal Mechanical Engineering Service PAM Product Registration Product Identification SON Rentage National Registry For Conformity Assessment Practitioners MANCAP Laboratory Services SONCAP Ports & Borders Training Services Library Inspectorate Compliance Directorate Management System Certification National Metrology Institute National Single Window (NSW) Reportgov.ng search Menu News Flow chart for the sales of NIS Standards By Maryam LamidoJune 13, 2024No Comments1 min read FLOWCHART FOR THE SALES NIS STANDARDS[1] Previous PostSON Confiscates Over 30 Million Naira Worth Of Fake Electrical Cables In Ekiti State Next PostSON, LASG & FTAN Partner to Boost Standardization in the Hospitality Sector Leave a Reply Cancel Reply Name * Email * Website Save my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment. Share Tweet Share Pin The Standards Organisation of Nigeria 52, Lome Crescent, Zone 7, Wuse, Abuja, FCT. Technical Committees Food & Agriculture Textile and Leather Chemical Technology Mechanical Electrotechnical Civil Services Trade Affairs Quick LinksManagement System Certification Meet The Management Team MANCAP International Product Certification SONCAP Privacy Policy Training Services LPG Follow SON Online facebook instagram twitter linkedin youtube \u00a9 2026 Standards Organisation of Nigeria. Site Map Close Menu Home About SON The Organisation Who We Are The Mandate Organogram Meet The Management Team Departments/Units ICT Finance & Accounts HR National Product Certification International Product Certification Inspectorate & Compliance Laboratory Services Legal/Council Marketing Management System Certification National Metrology Institute Corporate Affairs Regional Operations Internal Audit Planning, Research & Statistics Procurement General Services Standards Development Training Services Technical Committees Overview Standing National Technical Committees Chemical Technology Civil Electrotechnical Food & Agriculture Mechanical Services Textile and Leather Trade Affairs Services SON SLA\u2019s Training Services Digital Standards Platform SONCAP/IMPORT National Product Certification/Export MANCAP Standards Organisation of Nigeria Export Conformity Programme (SONEXCAP) Certification. Halal Certification Special Economic Zones Conformity Assessment Programme. SEZCAP). Product Identification Scheme. Service & Process Certification Division. Organic Production Certification. 35% Value Addition Service. Apply for Product Certification/Export MANCAP SONEXCAP Halal Certification. SEZCAP PIS Service & Process Certification Organic Production Certification 35% Value Addition Section Ports & Borders Library Services Mandatory Energy Labeling Scheme (SONMELS) Management System Certification Testing Services National Metrology Institute National Metrology Institute Calibration Price List Service Process Flow Chart Service Charges Testing Service Process Flow Chart Testing Service Charges SMEs Desk Standards PAM Inspectorate & Compliance NRCAP Resources Management Systems Certification SON-MSC ISO Audit Process Flowchart Impartiality Policy Client Database Service Charge Policies Turn Around Time Suspension, Refusal, Cancellation, Scope Reduction and Expansion Policy Policy on the Use of Management Systems Certification Mark and Logo Service Process Flow Chart Application Form Management Systems Certification Contract Terms and Conditions with Client Complaint & Appeals Procedure Complaints Form Enquiry Training Training Services Training Services 2026 Training Calendar Ports & Border Port & Border: Field Inspection Process & Charges Port & Border Service Process Flow Chart Library Library Service Process Flow Chart Media Center News & Updates Photo Gallery Staff Staff Mail ID Card HRM e-Receipt E-Store e-Service HELP Contact Us Contact SON Branch Locator FAQs SON FAQs PAM FAQ SONCAP FAQ MANCAP FAQ Product Registration FAQ Eder-Services SME Desk Portal Mechanical Engineering Service PAM Product Registration Product Identification SON Rentage National Registry For Conformity Assessment Practitioners MANCAP Laboratory Services SONCAP Ports & Borders Training Services Library Inspectorate Compliance Directorate Management System Certification National Metrology Institute National Single Window (NSW) Reportgov.ng Translate", "content_hash": "766c7bfeb264606730c68532f990a651d94ac2fa11a758fc2238c65d8661af9a", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:44.692086+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1888", "title": "SON Confiscates Over 30 Million Naira Worth Of Fake Electrical Cables In Ekiti State", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/13/son-confiscates-over-30-million-naira-worth-of-fake-electrical-cables-in-ekiti-state/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/13/son-confiscates-over-30-million-naira-worth-of-fake-electrical-cables-in-ekiti-state/", "text": "The Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) has seized counterfeit electrical cables and wires valued at over 30 million Naira in Ekiti State. The operation took place during a raid in several major markets following intelligence reports that some vendors were selling substandard cables. The SON taskforce sealed off several shops and confiscated the substandard items, loading them onto trucks for removal. Mr. Pius Manji, Director of the Inspectorate and Compliance Department at SON, briefed the press after the raid. Represented by Engr. Joel Aboyeji, Manji explained that the operation aimed to cleanse the markets of unsafe cables and wires. Manji noted that the substandard items were removed to prevent their circulation. He highlighted that the unscrupulous importers had cloned popular brands to deceive consumers, posing serious risks to households and potentially leading to fire outbreaks due to the use of substandard products. This practice also undermines local manufacturers and investments in the sector. He emphasized that SON is committed to ensuring that only quality products are available in the markets. The confiscated cables and wires will be destroyed, and SON will persist in prosecuting dealers who distribute substandard products. Manji warned that SON\u2019s enforcement team would continue to target importers and sellers of substandard electrical materials, urging electrical cable dealers to desist from such practices or face ongoing seizures and prosecution. Their actions, he stressed, not only sabotage and harm local industries and the economy but also endanger the lives of Nigerians.", "content_hash": "590fc6fc857621e01c3c724e58ce99bdb47c75803264046bdf7221c9ba60dde6", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:47.170913+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1889", "title": "30TH ARSO General Assembly Opens in Abuja", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/19/30th-arso-general-assembly-opens-in-abuja/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/19/30th-arso-general-assembly-opens-in-abuja/", "text": "Abuja, Nigeria \u2013 The 30th General Assembly of the African Organisation for Standardisation (ARSO) commenced on June 17, 2024, at the Abuja Continental Hotel. This landmark event, hosted by the Federal Government of Nigeria through the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), marks a significant gathering of standard bodies from across the African continent. The assembly opened with the ARSO Champions meeting, setting the stage for a series of discussions and engagements that will run until June 21, 2024. The event brings together industry leaders, policymakers, and experts dedicated to shaping Africa\u2019s standardisation landscape. A highlight of the event is the trade expo showcasing made-in-Nigeria goods, providing a platform for local manufacturers to exhibit their products to a diverse audience. This expo is a crucial part of the assembly, emphasizing the importance of standardisation in promoting Nigerian products and fostering economic growth. Participants will have the opportunity to gain insights, forge strategic partnerships, and contribute to Africa\u2019s sustainable development. The assembly underscores the critical role of standardisation in driving economic growth and enhancing trade across African nations.", "content_hash": "a803870d2d5d74b360ed480d467969890054da5f89ace249d15f1ce65c717a62", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:49.729507+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1890", "title": "ARSO General Assembly: SON DG Ifeanyi Okeke Meets with BSI Delegation", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/21/arso-general-assembly-son-dg-ifeanyi-okeke-meets-with-bsi-delegation/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/21/arso-general-assembly-son-dg-ifeanyi-okeke-meets-with-bsi-delegation/", "text": "In a notable development during the 30th African Organisation for Standardisation (ARSO) General Assembly, Dr. Ifeanyi Okeke, the Director General and Chief Executive of the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), engaged in a bilateral meeting with a high-level delegation from the British Standards Institute (BSI). DG/CE Dr. Ifeanyi Okeke and M. Volodymyr Yakubov of BSI The discussions focused on establishing a stronger partnership to evaluate the societal impacts of standardization activities. This partnership aims to enhance the effectiveness of standardization in driving economic growth, ensuring consumer safety, and promoting sustainable development. Dr. Okeke emphasized the importance of such collaborations in achieving global standardization goals and improving the quality of life across nations. DG SON Dr. Ifeanyi Okeke with ISO Deputy Secretary General Sylvio Dulinsky In addition to his meeting with the BSI delegation, Dr. Okeke also held a brief but significant discussion with the ISO delegation, led by Deputy Secretary-General Silvio Dulinsky. This meeting further underscored SON\u2019s commitment to international collaboration in standardization efforts. The exchange with ISO representatives aimed at aligning Nigeria\u2019s standardization practices with global benchmarks, thereby fostering greater international trade and cooperation. The 30th ARSO General Assembly has provided a critical platform for SON to engage with international partners, share insights, and develop strategies for improving standardization processes. These efforts are expected to have a lasting impact on the standardization landscape in Nigeria and across the African continent. Dr. Okeke expressed optimism about the outcomes of these meetings, highlighting that the strengthened partnerships with BSI and ISO will lead to more rigorous and impactful standardization activities. He reiterated SON\u2019s dedication to continuous improvement and adaptation of international best practices to meet local needs. The assembly continues to facilitate crucial dialogues among key stakeholders, aiming to advance the African Continental Free Trade Area (AfCFTA) and enhance economic integration through harmonized standards. See other pictures below", "content_hash": "33599e7d0cf3e11e3973e8133d2a74a42dc61f77b27b3b542e049d50e9c28515", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:18:53.664795+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1891", "title": "ARSO General Assembly Sees Landmark Collaboration between Standards Organisation of Nigeria and Standards Association of Zimbabwe", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/27/arso-general-assembly-sees-landmark-collaboration-between-standards-organization-of-nigeria-and-standards-association-of-zimbabwe/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/06/27/arso-general-assembly-sees-landmark-collaboration-between-standards-organization-of-nigeria-and-standards-association-of-zimbabwe/", "text": "At the 30th African Organisation for Standardisation (ARSO) General Assembly, a significant collaboration was initiated between the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) and the Standards Association of Zimbabwe (SAZ). Dr. Ifeanyi Okeke, the Director General and Chief Executive of SON, led a bilateral meeting with a high-level SAZ delegation led by Mr. Cosmos Mukoyi, the Acting Director General to explore potential areas of cooperation and strengthen mutual working relations. The meeting focused on fostering partnership in standardisation activities, with discussions spanning various domains such as quality and safety standards, system revenue improvement through inspection, certification, digitization, enforcement, and information sharing. Both parties aimed to learn from each other\u2019s experiences and enhance their respective endeavors. Dr. Ifeanyi Okeke expressed optimism about the collaboration, highlighting the importance of knowledge sharing, training, and revenue initiatives in addressing emerging challenges and achieving the organisations\u2019 objectives effectively. This partnership underscores the commitment of both nations to enhance their standards and quality assurance frameworks, contributing to the socio-economic development and well-being of their citizens.", "content_hash": "da7383ae9b13c6e493881160e08e5ffb6a54886f7b9614b3ff921c08fafd03f7", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:07.881369+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1892", "title": "BREAKING: Cristiano Ronaldo suspended by Portugal for 30 days, fined \u20ac255", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/breaking-cristiano-ronaldo-suspended-by-portugal-for-30-days-fined-255/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/breaking-cristiano-ronaldo-suspended-by-portugal-for-30-days-fined-255/", "text": "[Sport](https://dailypost.ng/sport-news/)BREAKING: Cristiano Ronaldo suspended by Portugal for 30 days, fined \u20ac255 Published on October 19, 2026By [Ifreke Inyang](https://dailypost.ng/author/ifreke-inyang/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/breaking-cristiano-ronaldo-suspended-by-portugal-for-30-days-fined-255/comments/) The Portuguese Football Federation has suspended national team captain Cristiano Ronaldo for 30 days and fined him \u20ac255 for leaving the team\u2019s camp in Denmark during the September international break.Football transfer expert Fabrizio Romano reported the development on X, stating that the decision followed Ronaldo\u2019s departure from the national team camp.\u201cCristiano Ronaldo has been suspended for 30 days plus fined for \u20ac255.\u201cThe decision has been made by Portugal Federation after he left the national team\u2019s camp in Denmark.Recommended[2026 Ballon d'Or: Thierry Henry confirmed as co-host](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/2026-ballon-dor-thierry-henry-confirmed-as-co-host/)[NPFL: Williams voted Enyimba's September Player of the Month](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/npfl-williams-voted-enyimbas-september-player-of-the-month/)[EPL: 'I don't care' - Ferdinand tells Carrick to always start Man Utd star](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/epl-i-dont-care-ferdinand-tells-carrick-to-always-start-man-utd-star-3/)\u201cCristiano himself had suggested a punishment after apologizing for that,\u201d Romano wrote.Ronaldo had left the camp ahead of Portugal\u2019s UEFA Nations League fixture against Denmark on September 30, following tensions with head coach Jorge Jesus.The forward later apologised for his actions and indicated that he was willing to accept punishment.The suspension is expected to allow Ronaldo to return for Portugal\u2019s November international fixtures, subject to his selection.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=BREAKING%3A%20Cristiano%20Ronaldo%20suspended%20by%20Portugal%20for%2030%20days%2C%20fined%20%E2%82%AC255%20%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F19%2Fbreaking-cristiano-ronaldo-suspended-by-portugal-for-30-days-fined-255%2F) FacebookYou may like[EPL table: Gary Neville states position Man Utd must finish this season](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/epl-table-gary-neville-states-position-man-utd-must-finish-this-season-3/)[Bauchi NDC guber candidate resigns from party](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/breaking-ndc-guber-candidate-dumps-party/)[UCL: Maresca gives injury updates on Haaland, Semenyo ahead AEK Athens clash](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/ucl-maresca-gives-injury-updates-on-haaland-semenyo-ahead-of-aek-athens-clash/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/breaking-cristiano-ronaldo-suspended-by-portugal-for-30-days-fined-255/comments/)", "content_hash": "48d37716486b01d1f5567d7e77a67f6f3ba29919790cd382e431020e26d1a0f6", "domain": "dailypost.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:10.075574+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1893", "title": "DG SON Moves to Strengthen Synergy with CEN-CENELEC, Holds Collaborative Meeting", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/09/11/dg-son-moves-to-strengthen-synergy-with-cen-cenelec-holds-collaborative-meeting/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/09/11/dg-son-moves-to-strengthen-synergy-with-cen-cenelec-holds-collaborative-meeting/", "text": "The Director General/ Chief Executive of the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke, held a collaborative meeting with the Director General of CEN-CENELEC Mrs. Elena Santiago and President of CENELEC, Mr. Stefano Caizouari, during the ongoing ISO annual meeting in Colombia. DG/CE SON Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okereke at the ISO Annual Meeting in Columbia CEN and CENELEC are international non \u2013 profit associations, that are officially recognized as European Standardization Organizations. CEN is the European Committee for Standardization that provide a platform for the development of European Standards and other specifications, while CENELEC is the European Committee for Electro-technical Standardization and is responsible for standardization in the electro-technical field. The meeting reached an understanding on improving the existing relationship between SON and CEN-CENELEC in the area of standardisation. Mrs. Elena Santiago who represents the CEN-CENELEC partnership explained that CEN mirrors ISO activities and is committed to using digitalisation to promote standardisation. The CEN-CENELEC team promised to grant SON access to the CEN-CENELEC database of standard with observers\u2019 status to standardisation activities and record. They further promised to include SON in the major European project in which more than 60% is focused on Africa. In his response, the SON Director General welcomed the support from CEN-CENELEC, affirming that SON would fully utilize the access to CEN-CENELEC\u2019s standards portal. He reiterated SON\u2019s dedication to enhancing Nigeria\u2019s position in global standardization through this partnership. The meeting ended with CEN-CENELEC delegation requesting that SON forward a mail detailing her demands for the CEN-CENELEC Board to consider at its November 2024 meeting. The partnership between SON and CEN-CENELEC strengthens Nigeria\u2019s involvement in international standardization. With access to European standards databases and participation in key projects, SON is set to influence global standards, particularly in Africa, while driving innovation and economic development through standardization efforts.", "content_hash": "e3c1e3adea67afc391c6ccedab8af1f1eb10ee0599c5bee9a9f485a00c04b9bd", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:15.572407+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1894", "title": "SON Celebrates African Day of Standardisation with Lunch of National Standards and Award Ceremony", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/09/18/son-celebrates-african-day-of-standardization-with-lunch-of-national-standards-and-award-ceremony/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/09/18/son-celebrates-african-day-of-standardization-with-lunch-of-national-standards-and-award-ceremony/", "text": "The Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) commemorated the African Day of Standardization with a grand event held in Abuja, which featured the official launching of several new national standards, including the much-anticipated Nigerian National Standardization Strategy (NNSS). The event also recognized outstanding young minds through an award ceremony for the winners of the National Standardization Essay and Quiz Competition. The event, which drew stakeholders from various sectors, was graced by top government officials and industry leaders. The Honourable Minister of Industry, Trade, and Investment (FMITI) was represented by the Permanent Secretary of the Ministry Ambassador Nura Abba Rimi, underscoring the government\u2019s commitment to supporting national standardization efforts and the implementation of best practices across all sectors of the economy. The launching of the NNSS marked a significant milestone for Nigeria\u2019s standardization landscape, as it aims to provide a clear strategic framework for the development, promotion, and adoption of standards across industries, fostering innovation and economic growth. In his remarks, the Permanent Secretary of FMITI commended SON for its pivotal role in driving the nation\u2019s standardization agenda and emphasized the importance of standards in ensuring product quality, consumer safety, and the competitiveness of Nigerian goods in the global market. Other dignitaries in attendance included heads of various government agencies and regulatory bodies, who reiterated their support for SON\u2019s initiatives and the critical role of standards in achieving Nigeria\u2019s industrialization goals. The event concluded with the presentation of prizes to the winners of the National Standardization Essay and Quiz Competition. The competition, organized annually by SON, aims to raise awareness among students about the importance of standardization in national development, while fostering a culture of quality and innovation among the younger generation. SON\u2019s Director-General Dr. Ifeanyi Okeke, in his address, highlighted the importance of continued collaboration between stakeholders in both the public and private sectors to ensure the successful implementation of the newly launched standards and strategies. He also applauded the student participants for their exemplary understanding of standardization concepts and urged them to continue contributing to the nation\u2019s standardization efforts. The African Day of Standardization serves as an important platform for African countries to unite in their shared mission of advancing regional integration through the harmonization and adoption of international standards, with Nigeria continuing to play a leading role in this effort.", "content_hash": "d6f41df2be12b2946f01b9e678d5e49fbdd598d7421d63f305e41012aafde37b", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:22.307749+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1895", "title": "National Single Window Project Team, Visits SON for an Interactive Session, to Advance the Renewed Hope Agenda", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/09/19/national-single-window-project-team-visits-son-for-an-interactive-session-to-advance-the-renewed-hope-agenda/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/09/19/national-single-window-project-team-visits-son-for-an-interactive-session-to-advance-the-renewed-hope-agenda/", "text": "Single Window (NSW) project team, led by Mr. Uthman Aminu of West Blue Consulting, visited the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) on September recently. The visit was aimed at fostering In a significant step towards improving Nigeria\u2019s trade facilitation and regulatory efficiency, the National collaboration in line with the \u201cRenewed Hope\u201d agenda of President Bola Ahmed Tinubu, which seeks to enhance transparency, ease of doing business and economic growth in Nigeria. The session primarily focused on the Business Process Analysis stream, with key contributions from the Technology and Legal/Regulatory streams, ensuring a comprehensive approach to addressing challenges in trade regulation. Through this collaboration, the NSW team gained crucial insights into the operational flow of SON\u2019s Conformity Assessment Programme (SONCAP), a vital mechanism for ensuring the quality and safety of imported goods. The NSW project, designed to simplify and integrate trade processes across multiple agencies, aligns with the government\u2019s drive to improve Nigeria\u2019s global competitiveness. By streamlining procedures and reducing bottlenecks in the SONCAP scheme, this partnership aims to facilitate faster clearances, ensure regulatory compliance, and protect consumers from substandard goods. The successful engagement between SON and the NSW project team underscores the importance of inter-agency collaboration in achieving the President\u2019s Economic Agenda. By leveraging technology and process optimization, the partnership will contribute to creating a more business-friendly environment in Nigeria, enhancing trade efficiency, and bolstering investor confidence in the Nation\u2019s regulatory framework.", "content_hash": "256fb4f57fee9623c4d6ceef71643331d3275c0ed4e46c14f4d87c3ab2a5906e", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:31.125421+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1896", "title": "2027: Our people should defend their votes - Ohanaeze warns election riggers", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/2027-our-people-should-defend-their-votes-ohanaeze-warns-election-riggers/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/2027-our-people-should-defend-their-votes-ohanaeze-warns-election-riggers/", "text": "[Politics](https://dailypost.ng/politics/)2027: Our people should defend their votes - Ohanaeze warns election riggersPublished on October 19, 2026By [Casmir Nwankwo](https://dailypost.ng/author/casmir-nwankwo/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/2027-our-people-should-defend-their-votes-ohanaeze-warns-election-riggers/comments/)The apex Igbo socio-cultural organisation, Ohanaeze Ndigbo, has issued a stern warning to politicians, political parties and electoral officials against any attempt to manipulate the 2027 general elections by undermining the constitutional right of Ndigbo to freely elect their leaders.Ohanaeze declared unequivocally that Ndigbo would not accept the theft of their votes, the imposition of unwanted political leaders or any deliberate attempt to subvert their collective democratic will.The organisation insisted that no governor, political party, electoral official or influential politician was above the law or had the right to determine the political future of the people against their wishes.It warned that anyone who conspired to rig the 2027 elections in Igboland should expect determined resistance from an electorate that was increasingly conscious of its democratic rights.Recommended[2027: 'Tinubu doing politics, wickedness since becoming president' - Atiku's aide replies Alake](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/2027-tinubu-doing-politics-wickedness-since-becoming-president-atikus-aide-replies-alake/)[2027: Only POS business this govt has given you - ADC urges Nigerians to reject APC](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/2027-only-pos-business-this-govt-has-given-you-adc-urges-nigerians-to-reject-apc/)[2027: Tinubu's campaigner, Showunmi defends wife's new INEC role](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/inec-appointment-tinubus-campaigner-showunmi-opens-up-on-wifes-new-role/)Ohanaeze called on Igbo youths, traditional rulers, community leaders, civil society organisations and other stakeholders to remain vigilant, mobilise eligible voters and defend the integrity of the ballot through lawful, peaceful and constitutionally recognised means.The warning extends to Abia, Anambra, Ebonyi, Enugu and Imo states, as well as Igbo-speaking communities in Delta State, including Anioma, and Rivers State, including Ikwerre communities.The pan-Igbo organisation insisted that every eligible voter deserved the freedom to cast a ballot without intimidation, coercion, vote-buying, ballot snatching or manipulation of election results.This was contained in a statement issued on Monday by the factional Deputy President-General, Mazi Okechukwu Isiguzoro, and Professor Chibuikeya Achoakawa, and made available to journalists.The statement said the Imeobi, the highest decision-making organ of Ohanaeze Ndigbo Worldwide, had approved the organisation\u2019s proposed Igbo Blueprint for the 2027 elections, which prioritises massive voter participation, electoral accountability, political consciousness and the protection of the people\u2019s mandate.Ohanaeze urged Ndigbo to reject voter apathy, obtain their Permanent Voter Cards, participate actively in the electoral process and remain vigilant throughout voting, counting, collation and the announcement of results.The organisation called on the Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) to guarantee transparent, free, fair and credible elections in which the final results reflect the actual votes cast.Invoking the cultural symbolism of the Nz\u1ecdgbu Nz\u1ecdgbu spirit and the traditional Amadioha deity, Ohanaeze declared that the Igbo people\u2019s determination to resist injustice and defend their dignity must not be underestimated.The organisation stressed that these cultural references represented the collective resolve of Ndigbo to reject oppression, political manipulation and the deliberate suppression of their democratic rights.Ohanaeze further called on Ndigbo to vote according to their consciences and assess every candidate on merit, integrity, competence, performance and commitment to the collective interests of the people.It said politicians who had failed to fulfil their promises, neglected their constituencies or abused public trust should not expect automatic electoral support merely because of their party affiliations.The organisation also demanded accountability in local government administration and urged voters to scrutinise the management of public funds. It said any proven diversion or misappropriation of local government allocations must be investigated and those responsible made to face the consequences prescribed by law.Ohanaeze warned prospective election riggers that political influence, financial power and public office would not excuse electoral crimes.It called on the National Assembly to strengthen electoral legislation, close loopholes that facilitate malpractice and ensure the effective investigation and prosecution of offenders, with appropriate penalties imposed in accordance with the Constitution and due process.\u201cOhanaeze\u2019s position is clear: the votes of Ndigbo belong to the people, not to politicians or political parties. No individual has the right to steal the people\u2019s mandate, and no political ambition justifies the subversion of democracy,\u201d the statement said.The organisation called on all stakeholders to ensure that the 2027 elections became a defining moment for democratic accountability in Igboland. It urged Ndigbo to remain united, vigilant and determined to exercise their constitutional rights without fear or intimidation.\u201cThe message to election riggers is unequivocal: Ndigbo will not surrender their votes, their dignity or their democratic future. The spirit of Nz\u1ecdgbu Nz\u1ecdgbu and the symbolism of Amadioha stand as powerful reminders of a people\u2019s determination to resist injustice.\u201cAnyone who attempts to manipulate the ballot must be prepared to answer for their actions under the law. In 2027, the people\u2019s mandate must prevail,\u201d the statement added.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=2027%3A%20Our%20people%20should%20defend%20their%20votes%20-%20Ohanaeze%20warns%20election%20riggers%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F19%2F2027-our-people-should-defend-their-votes-ohanaeze-warns-election-riggers%2F) FacebookYou may like[Ex-Minority Whip seeks to overturn judgment nullifying Gombe APC Primary](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/jc-appeals-court-ruling-nullifying-gombe-re-election-ticket/)['DSS DG a coward, Joe Igbokwe lost his mind long ago' - Sowore](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/dss-dg-coward-joe-igbokwe-lost-his-mind-long-ago-sowore/)[Atiku cannot rely on Hausa, Fulani votes to beat Tinubu - APC chieftain Kwankwaso](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/atiku-cannot-rely-on-hausa-fulani-votes-to-beat-tinubu-apc-chieftain/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/2027-our-people-should-defend-their-votes-ohanaeze-warns-election-riggers/comments/)", "content_hash": "296fc84bd03e78ec3c2da27cadb1950d5fef4d4b4f29566ae2166c6ecca1b59b", "domain": "dailypost.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:34.607676+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1897", "title": "SON\u2019s Training Service Department Empowers Businesses with ISO 10002 Course", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/11/06/sons-training-service-department-empowers-businesses-with-iso-10002-course/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/11/06/sons-training-service-department-empowers-businesses-with-iso-10002-course/", "text": "SON\u2019s TRAINING SERVICES DEPARTMENT EMPOWERS BUSINESSES WITH ISO 10002 COURSE The Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) recently hosted a successful ISO 10002/2018 \u2013 Customer Satisfaction and Complaint Handling course, where participants from the United Bank of Africa (UBA) and Dele Pharmaceutical Group (HMA Medical Fluids) gained invaluable insights into effective complaint management practices. Throughout the training, participants engaged in discussions and practical exercises emphasizing the importance of transforming complaints into opportunities. They learned strategies for building stronger customer relationships and driving continuous improvement within their organizations. The ISO 10002 training program offers a range of benefits that can transform how organizations handle customer complaints. Participants learn how to enhance customer satisfaction, improve their organizational reputation, and significantly reduce negative impacts on branding. As businesses increasingly prioritize exceptional customer service, SON\u2019s training programs emerge as vital resources for professional development in effective complaint management. Organizations looking to elevate their customer service standards and refine their complaint management strategies are encouraged to contact SON\u2019s Training Services Department for details on upcoming ISO 10002 courses. Investing in training today can pave the way for a more customer-centric future!", "content_hash": "a5af61f3c695291c05f2f2a4dea4fa70e9fb611a66a3cff026b5a1bbd198bfe4", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:19:50.285806+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1898", "title": "SON ORGANIZED NATIONAL CONFERENCE ON BUILDING CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY, EMPHASIZES STANDARD PRACTICES AS KEY TO SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/11/13/son-organized-national-conference-on-building-construction-industry-emphasizes-standard-practices-as-key-to-sustainable-development/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/11/13/son-organized-national-conference-on-building-construction-industry-emphasizes-standard-practices-as-key-to-sustainable-development/", "text": "SON ORGANIZED NATIONAL CONFERENCE ON BUILDING CONSTRUCTION INDUSTRY, EMPHASIZES STANDARD PRACTICES AS KEY TO SUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT The National Conference on the Building Construction Industry, hosted by the Director General of the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), Dr. Ifeanyi C. Okeke brought together prominent leaders, stakeholders, and professionals from across the construction sector. Themed \u201cAdherence to Standard Practices \u2013 Bedrock of Sustainable Development in the Building Construction Industry,\u201d the conference underscored the critical importance of adherence to Standards for the safety, sustainability, and growth of Nigeria\u2019s building industry. The Honorable Minister of State for Industry, in the Federal Ministry of Industry, Trade, and Investment, Senator John Owan Enoh declared the Conference Open. In his remarks, the Minister emphasized the urgent need for cooperation across the construction industry to enhance safety measures and prevent the tragic building collapses that have become all too common in recent years. He called on industry stakeholders, regulatory bodies, and professionals to prioritize compliance with established standards to secure public safety and foster sustainable development within the sector. The event saw a huge turnout from construction professionals, stakeholders, and representatives of regulatory bodies, all of whom engaged in discussions on how adherence to standards can support Nigeria\u2019s economic growth and infrastructural development. Experts from various fields presented papers covering critical issues, including best practices in building design, structural integrity, sustainable materials, and risk management. A highlight of the conference was the panel discussion, which featured notable voices from professional bodies, government regulatory agencies, and key players in the construction industry. The panelists shared insights into current challenges, innovative solutions, and best practices, driving home the message that building safety and sustainability are shared responsibilities across the industry. At the conclusion of the conference, a communique outlining key resolutions was agreed on, including recommendations for stricter enforcement of building standards, the need for enhanced collaboration among regulatory bodies, and strategies for improving public awareness about the importance of construction standards. The communique reaffirmed SON\u2019s commitment to working alongside industry players to foster a culture of safety and excellence in Nigeria\u2019s building sector. The National Conference on the Building Construction Industry represents a pivotal step toward aligning Nigeria\u2019s construction practices with global standards, ensuring that the country\u2019s infrastructure development remains safe, sustainable, and resilient. Mrs. Bolaji, Director Public Relations", "content_hash": "90e609bc56a825c9a8e591938bccf8514fda154d05cb13156e2c25f479cccc7d", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:20:05.664891+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1899", "title": "12th Continental Essay Competition on Standardisation 2024/2025", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/11/29/12th-continental-essay-competition-on-standardisation-2024-2025/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/11/29/12th-continental-essay-competition-on-standardisation-2024-2025/", "text": "12th Continental Essay Competition on Standardisation 2024/2025 \u2013 Standards Organisation of Nigeria Skip to main content Hit enter to search or ESC to close Close Search search Menu Home About SON The Organisation Who We Are The Mandate Organogram Meet The Management Team Departments/Units ICT Finance & Accounts HR National Product Certification International Product Certification Inspectorate & Compliance Laboratory Services Legal/Council Marketing Management System Certification National Metrology Institute Corporate Affairs Regional Operations Internal Audit Planning, Research & Statistics Procurement General Services Standards Development Training Services Technical Committees Overview Standing National Technical Committees Chemical Technology Civil Electrotechnical Food & Agriculture Mechanical Services Textile and Leather Trade Affairs Services SON SLA\u2019s Training Services Digital Standards Platform SONCAP/IMPORT National Product Certification/Export MANCAP Standards Organisation of Nigeria Export Conformity Programme (SONEXCAP) Certification. Halal Certification Special Economic Zones Conformity Assessment Programme. SEZCAP). Product Identification Scheme. Service & Process Certification Division. Organic Production Certification. 35% Value Addition Service. Apply for Product Certification/Export MANCAP SONEXCAP Halal Certification. SEZCAP PIS Service & Process Certification Organic Production Certification 