7, Wuse, Abuja, FCT. Technical Committees Food & Agriculture Textile and Leather Chemical Technology Mechanical Electrotechnical Civil Services Trade Affairs Quick LinksManagement System Certification Meet The Management Team MANCAP International Product Certification SONCAP Privacy Policy Training Services LPG Follow SON Online facebook instagram twitter linkedin youtube \u00a9 2026 Standards Organisation of Nigeria. Site Map Close Menu Home About SON The Organisation Who We Are The Mandate Organogram Meet The Management Team Departments/Units ICT Finance & Accounts HR National Product Certification International Product Certification Inspectorate & Compliance Laboratory Services Legal/Council Marketing Management System Certification National Metrology Institute Corporate Affairs Regional Operations Internal Audit Planning, Research & Statistics Procurement General Services Standards Development Training Services Technical Committees Overview Standing National Technical Committees Chemical Technology Civil Electrotechnical Food & Agriculture Mechanical Services Textile and Leather Trade Affairs Services SON SLA\u2019s Training Services Digital Standards Platform SONCAP/IMPORT National Product Certification/Export MANCAP Standards Organisation of Nigeria Export Conformity Programme (SONEXCAP) Certification. Halal Certification Special Economic Zones Conformity Assessment Programme. SEZCAP). Product Identification Scheme. Service & Process Certification Division. Organic Production Certification. 35% Value Addition Service. Apply for Product Certification/Export MANCAP SONEXCAP Halal Certification. SEZCAP PIS Service & Process Certification Organic Production Certification 35% Value Addition Section Ports & Borders Library Services Mandatory Energy Labeling Scheme (SONMELS) Management System Certification Testing Services National Metrology Institute National Metrology Institute Calibration Price List Service Process Flow Chart Service Charges Testing Service Process Flow Chart Testing Service Charges SMEs Desk Standards PAM Inspectorate & Compliance NRCAP Resources Management Systems Certification SON-MSC ISO Audit Process Flowchart Impartiality Policy Client Database Service Charge Policies Turn Around Time Suspension, Refusal, Cancellation, Scope Reduction and Expansion Policy Policy on the Use of Management Systems Certification Mark and Logo Service Process Flow Chart Application Form Management Systems Certification Contract Terms and Conditions with Client Complaint & Appeals Procedure Complaints Form Enquiry Training Training Services Training Services 2026 Training Calendar Ports & Border Port & Border: Field Inspection Process & Charges Port & Border Service Process Flow Chart Library Library Service Process Flow Chart Media Center News & Updates Photo Gallery Staff Staff Mail ID Card HRM e-Receipt E-Store e-Service HELP Contact Us Contact SON Branch Locator FAQs SON FAQs PAM FAQ SONCAP FAQ MANCAP FAQ Product Registration FAQ Eder-Services SME Desk Portal Mechanical Engineering Service PAM Product Registration Product Identification SON Rentage National Registry For Conformity Assessment Practitioners MANCAP Laboratory Services SONCAP Ports & Borders Training Services Library Inspectorate Compliance Directorate Management System Certification National Metrology Institute National Single Window (NSW) Reportgov.ng Translate", "content_hash": "481379f35a9a2234a0edb5c825f1c212ea36e0fe87b3b880a2330d519146ecd6", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:20:52.330256+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1901", "title": "SON moves to Strengthen Nigeria\u2019s Urban Planning Regulations and Standards", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/15/son-moves-to-strengthen-nigerias-urban-planning-regulations-and-standards/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/15/son-moves-to-strengthen-nigerias-urban-planning-regulations-and-standards/", "text": "In its efforts to strengthen Nigeria\u2019s Urban Planning Regulations and Standards, the Director General/ Chief Executive of the Standards Organisation of Nigeria, Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke led a delegation for a meeting with the International Organization for Standardization /International Electrotechnical Commission Joint Technical Committee 1/Working Group 11 (ISO/IECJTC 1/WG 311) Smart Cities in Australia. The objective of the meeting is to provide SON with access to international frameworks and best practices for ensuring quality and safety in urban development. The Director General noted that by integrating these standards into local urban planning and construction processes, SON intends to strengthen its regulatory framework to combat the use of substandard building materials in the country. During the meeting, the Director General discussed issues regarding holistic urban development, supported by advanced ICT solutions that will enable better monitoring and enforcement of compliance with building standards. Deliberations during the meeting also elaborately explored the adoption of innovative technologies for testing and certi certification of construction materials. Through these efforts, SON will be better equipped to address the root causes of building collapse, enhance public safety, and support the development of resilient and sustainable urban spaces.", "content_hash": "73c27be924e7612dc86a224c59362878969d0d237d54dc929a0071b498487963", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:21:05.977996+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1902", "title": "SON Hosts Technical Committee Meeting on Tobacco and Similar Products in Abuja", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/19/son-hosts-technical-committee-meeting-on-tobacco-and-similar-products-in-abuja/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/19/son-hosts-technical-committee-meeting-on-tobacco-and-similar-products-in-abuja/", "text": "SON HOSTS TECHNICAL COMMITTEE MEETING ON TOBACCO AND SIMILAR PRODUCTS IN ABUJA Following the need to regulate the production of Tobacco and related products in Nigeria, and ensuring safety in line with International best practices, the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) convened a Technical Committee Meeting on Standards for Heated Tobacco Products (HTP), E-Cigarettes, and Nicotine Pouches at its Corporate Headquarters in Abuja. Declaring the meeting open, the Director General/ Chief Executive SON, Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke stressed the need to continuously align the requirements in the Nigerian Industrial Standards (NIS) for tobacco products with relevant international regulations to position Nigeria as a leader in the responsible regulation of tobacco and similar products. The Director General, represented by the Director, Standards Development, Engr. Yahaya Bukar emphasized that the standards will ensure safety and quality and mitigate health risks. He praised the committee for achieving significant milestones, including the elaboration of nine complex draft standards within a short period. The SON helmsman reaffirmed SON\u2019s commitment to public health-driven regulation. According to him, these efforts would position Nigeria as a leader in the responsible regulation of tobacco and similar products as well as bolster consumer confidence in the Nigerian market. Discussions during the meeting covered critical issues such as reducing the risks of substandard products, improving transparency, and setting technical guidelines for manufacturers. The meeting concluded with stakeholders pledging support for the adoption and implementation of the new standards. The Committee was chaired by Professor Adeleke C. Adebayo of the Obafemi Awolowo University, Ile-Ife with membership drawn from key organizations such as British American Tobacco (BAT), Philip Morris International, Japan Tobacco International, and regulatory agencies including the National Agency for Food and Drug Administration and Control (NAFDAC), Nigeria Customs Service, and the Federal Ministry of Industry, Trade and Investment (FMITI). The meeting underscores SON\u2019s unwavering commitment to ensuring public health, consumer safety, and regulatory excellence in response to the evolving landscape of tobacco and nicotine products.", "content_hash": "7b88120ed95edae5b4cdd87b71c72fdcd21958ae21758f38d511e608793fb2cf", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:21:14.364234+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1903", "title": "NAF neutralises terrorist figures in precision air strike", "url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/naf-neutralizes-terrorist-figures-in-precision-air-strike/", "final_url": "https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/naf-neutralizes-terrorist-figures-in-precision-air-strike/", "text": "[News](https://dailypost.ng/hot-news/)NAF neutralises terrorist figures in precision air strikePublished on October 19, 2026By [John Gabriel](https://dailypost.ng/author/john-gabriel/)[Comment](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/naf-neutralizes-terrorist-figures-in-precision-air-strike/comments/)The Nigerian Air Force (NAF), operating under the Joint Task Force, Operation HADIN KAI (OPHK), has recorded a significant operational success against terrorists in the Lake Chad region following a precision air strike on an identified terrorist hideout on October 19, 2026.This was contained in a statement by Air Commodore Ehimen Ejodame, Director of Public Relations and Information, Headquarters, Nigerian Air Force.According to the statement, the operation underscores the NAF\u2019s sustained commitment to degrading terrorist networks, disrupting their logistics and enhancing security across Nigeria\u2019s North-East.\"Preliminary post-strike assessments indicate that several prominent Islamic State West Africa Province (ISWAP) fighters were neutralised, including individuals identified as key figures within the group\u2019s security structure and leadership council, like Jindullah, reportedly the Chief Security Guard and confidant of Abu Saleem as well as Abul Kissa, a member of ISWAP Shura Council,\" the statement said.Recommended[Osun police declare Nurudeen Alowonle, Sibi wanted over Emir's murder](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/osun-police-declare-nurudeen-alowonle-sibi-wanted-over-emirs-murder/)[N66bn erosion fund awaits Tinubu\u2019s approval \u2013 Ndume](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/n66bn-erosion-fund-awaits-tinubus-approval-ndume/)[If Buhari as general couldn't end insecurity, don't expect Tinubu to \u2013 Abdulaziz Yari](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/if-buhari-as-general-couldnt-end-insecurity-dont-expect-tinubu-to-abdulaziz-yari/)It said the strike also destroyed logistical assets, including boat engines and motorcycles, believed to support the group\u2019s movement and operational activities.It said the operation demonstrates the NAF\u2019s intense effort to conduct intelligence-led precision strikes against terrorist enclaves concealed within difficult terrain, by neutralising key operatives and destroying critical logistical resources.According to the statement, the strike delivers a significant setback to ISWAP\u2019s operational capability, further constraining its ability to coordinate activities and threaten vulnerable communities.The Chief of the Air Staff, Air Marshal Sunday Kelvin Aneke, reaffirmed the NAF\u2019s resolve to sustain decisive air operations against terrorist networks in support of ongoing efforts to restore peace and stability across the country.\"The Nigerian Air Force remained committed to working closely with sister Services and other security agencies to consolidate operational gains, protect vulnerable communities and advance efforts towards lasting peace and security in the North-East,\" it further said.Share this story[WhatsApp](https://wa.me/?text=NAF%20neutralises%20terrorist%20figures%20in%20precision%20air%20strike%20https%3A%2F%2Fdailypost.ng%2F2026%2F10%2F19%2Fnaf-neutralizes-terrorist-figures-in-precision-air-strike%2F) FacebookYou may like[Nigeria, Rwanda to expand military training, defence production](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/nigeria-rwanda-move-to-expand-military-training-defence-production-3/)[Gov Namadi promises improved welfare, renovation of Jigawa NYSC camp](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/gov-namadi-promises-improved-welfare-renovation-of-jigawa-nysc-camp/)[Tinubu mourns death of ex-Delta Gov, Uduaghan](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/tinubu-mourns-death-of-ex-delta-gov-uduaghan/)[Join the conversation](https://dailypost.ng/2026/10/19/naf-neutralizes-terrorist-figures-in-precision-air-strike/comments/)", "content_hash": "8e905c32bbda6bfdbbebb4c31ef616f546d728d27dc6af70900d70c761258d49", "domain": "dailypost.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:21:52.840840+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1904", "title": "SON DG Calls for Swift Action on MOU as NMDPRA CEO Pays Him a Visit", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/20/son-dg-calls-for-swift-action-on-mou-as-nmdpra-ceo-pays-him-a-visit/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/20/son-dg-calls-for-swift-action-on-mou-as-nmdpra-ceo-pays-him-a-visit/", "text": "SON DG CALLS FOR SWIFT ACTION ON MOU AS NMDPRA CEO PAYS HIM A VISIT The Director-General of the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke, warmly welcomed the Chief Executive Officer of the Nigerian Midstream and Downstream Petroleum Regulatory Authority (NMDPRA), Engr. Farouk Ahmed, and his team during their strategic visit to SON. Dr. Okeke expressed his delight at the cordial and productive relationship between the two organisations emphasizing its significance in advancing Nigeria\u2019s petroleum sector. He lauded the collaboration so far and reiterated the importance of expediting efforts to finalize their Memorandum of Understanding (MoU). During the meeting, both parties agreed on the necessity of reviewing key specifications, particularly concerning modular refineries. Stakeholders emphasized the importance of aligning plans and concepts with practical considerations, especially regarding Sulphur content in petroleum products, to ensure that standards are both achievable and effective. Safety standards also took center stage, with consensus reached on measures such as the colorization of petroleum products to enhance identification and compliance. It was recommended that a clear timeline for adherence to these standards be established to guide the industry. Both leaders agreed that the immediate implementation of ready standards is crucial, as any delays could potentially disrupt operations in the petroleum sector. The visit further reinforced the commitment of both SON and NMDPRA to strengthen their partnership, with a shared goal of ensuring compliance, enhancing safety, and fostering sustainable practices in Nigeria\u2019s petroleum industry.", "content_hash": "dcd1f5f43fc7280a174939a9ce44174af467e07beb6b6b32f11afad1dd9728ff", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:21:59.752203+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1905", "title": "SON Committed to the Promotion and Growth of African Traditional Medicine (ATM)", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/20/son-committed-to-the-promotion-and-growth-of-african-traditional-medicine-atm/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/20/son-committed-to-the-promotion-and-growth-of-african-traditional-medicine-atm/", "text": "SON COMMITTED TO THE PROMOTION AND GROWTH OF AFRICAN TRADITIONAL MEDICINE (ATM) The Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) has affirmed its commitment to promoting products that will compete favorably in the international market. The commitment was made during the 18th National Technical Mirror Committee meeting on African traditional Medicine (ATM) held in Lagos. In his opening remarks, the Director General and Chief Executive Dr; Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke thanked the Vice Chancellor, Professor Ibiyemi I. Olatunji-Bello, and the Management of Lagos State University (LASU) for graciously hosting the technical committee within the prestigious university premises and providing the necessary support for the meeting. The DG represented by the Director Standards Development Engr. Yahaya Bukar expressed his appreciation to the Coordinator and Chairperson of the committee, Prof. Maurice Iwu, whose intellectual prowess and unwavering commitment has ensured the success of the project since its inception in August 2015. Dr. Okeke noted that through the efforts of the National Technical Committee, Nigeria has pioneered the development and adoption of ten African Regional Standards for Traditional Medicine. He expressed hope that by the end of the meeting, an additional 14 ARS Standards will be adopted as Nigeria\u2019s National Standards, bringing the total to twenty-four (24). The SON\u2019s helmsman acknowledged the significant achievement gained by the TC considering Nigeria\u2019s previous status in the area of formulating standards for traditional medicine. He said the works carried out on these Standards has set Nigeria at the forefront of the promotion and development of African Traditional medicine. While commending the efforts of the NTC, he assured them that SON will play its role in ensuring the promotion of these standards for local and global promotion of Nigeria\u2019s Traditional Medicines. The DG noted that the National Standards developed by the NTC are crucial for global access to Nigerian products as they will facilitate compatibility, ensure quality, and reduce barriers across global markets. These standards will provide benchmarks for quality and safety, building trust among consumers and businesses. According to the DG SON, the NTC work will enable Nigerian traditional medicines to easily comply with international regulatory requirements, as many countries require imported goods to meet specific standards; He said the adoption of harmonized international standards by Nigeria is to simplify compliance, thus reducing the risk of Nigerian products being rejected or facing trade restrictions. He therefore urged all the professionals and experts present to contribute their best to accomplish the objectives outlined for the meeting. In similar vein, the Vice Chancellor of the Lagos State University (LASU), represented by The Deputy Vice Chancellor (Admin) Prof Adenike Omotunde in her welcome remarks noted that the occasion holds great significance as it is a gathering that will foster collaborations and sharing of ideas that will propel the development and regulation of traditional Medicine in Nigeria. She commended the work SON is doing to set standards, improve quality practices, and ensure the safety and efficacy of traditional remedies for the future of healthcare in the country. She looked forward to fruitful discussions and productive interactions that will arise from the engagement. Also speaking at the meeting, the chairperson of the SON NM/TC on African Traditional Medicine, Prof. Maurice Iwu urged all participants to work assiduously to develop as many standards as they can to be able to compete favorably with India and China in traditional African medicine for its utilization by generations and for national economic development.", "content_hash": "6d7d1752da5c7735d4186390a7c009c08db79644c436ed6fbc6cc63d89f2a8fb", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:22:11.131481+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1906", "title": "SON DG Honored with Doctoral Fellowship in Crisis and Disaster Management at the Nigeria Conference", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/23/son-dg-honored-with-doctoral-fellowship-in-crisis-and-disaster-management-at-the-nigeria-conference/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2024/12/23/son-dg-honored-with-doctoral-fellowship-in-crisis-and-disaster-management-at-the-nigeria-conference/", "text": "SON DG HONORED WITH DOCTORAL FELLOWSHIP IN CRISIS AND DISASTER MANAGEMENT AT THE NIGERIA CLIMATE CONFERENCE The Director General, Chief Executive of the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON), Dr. Ifeanyi Chukwunonso Okeke, has been awarded an Honorary Doctoral Fellowship by the Emergency, Crisis & Disaster Risk Management Institute (ECRIM). The award was presented during the maiden edition of the Nigeria Climate & Emergency Conference. Representing the SON DG at the event, Dr. Ganiyat Adebayo, Group Head of Environment Standards, delivered a goodwill message, expressing gratitude to the organizers for the recognition. Dr. Okeke emphasized the critical need for proactive measures to combat the climate crisis and mitigate associated risks. \u201cResilience and adaptation are not just strategies; they are imperatives for safeguarding our environment, protecting lives and livelihoods, and ensuring sustainable development,\u201d he said. Dr. Okeke highlighted the pivotal role of standardization in addressing climate challenges, noting that SON actively develops and enforces guidelines to promote sustainable practices across various sectors, including agriculture, energy, infrastructure, and waste management. He reaffirmed SON\u2019s unwavering commitment to fostering innovations that reduce greenhouse gas emissions and creating a safer, more sustainable Nigeria. \u201cSON remains a reliable partner in advancing Nigeria\u2019s climate response goals and will continue to support initiatives that prioritize sustainability, environmental stewardship, and global best practices,\u201d he added. In response, Dr. Chuks Akawo, Director-General of ECRIM, commended Dr. Okeke for his dedication and leadership in steering SON toward achieving its mandate and for contributing significantly to Nigeria\u2019s climate resilience and sustainability efforts.", "content_hash": "1c5c42ae1f084b20120d0c8ecc8c933c222ef50593c7eb1d1ce8bb2a4acd1635", "domain": "son.gov.ng", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T05:22:49.314637+00:00", "language": ""}, {"id": "1907", "title": "Public Alert on Expiration of Liquidified Petroleum Gas Steel Cylinders in Line with Nigeria Industrial Standard NIS 69:2013", "url": "https://son.gov.ng/2025/01/14/public-alert-on-expiration-of-liquidified-petroleum-gas-steel-cylinders-in-line-with-nigeria-industrial-standard-nis-692013/", "final_url": "https://son.gov.ng/2025/01/14/public-alert-on-expiration-of-liquidified-petroleum-gas-steel-cylinders-in-line-with-nigeria-industrial-standard-nis-692013/", "text": "Public Alert on Expiration of Liquidified Petroleum Gas Steel Cylinders in Line with Nigeria Industrial Standard NIS 69:2013 \u2013 Standards Organisation of Nigeria Skip to main content Hit enter to search or ESC to close Close Search search Menu Home About SON The Organisation Who We Are The Mandate Organogram Meet The Management Team Departments/Units ICT Finance & Accounts HR National Product Certification International Product Certification Inspectorate & Compliance Laboratory Services Legal/Council Marketing Management System Certification National Metrology Institute Corporate Affairs Regional Operations Internal Audit Planning, Research & Statistics Procurement General Services Standards Development Training Services Technical Committees Overview Standing National Technical Committees Chemical Technology Civil Electrotechnical Food & Agriculture Mechanical Services Textile and Leather Trade Affairs Services SON SLA\u2019s Training Services Digital Standards Platform SONCAP/IMPORT National Product Certification/Export MANCAP Standards Organisation of Nigeria Export Conformity Programme (SONEXCAP) Certification. Halal Certification Special Economic Zones Conformity Assessment Programme. SEZCAP). Product Identification Scheme. Service & Process Certification Division. Organic Production Certification. 35% Value Addition Service. Apply for Product Certification/Export MANCAP SONEXCAP Halal Certification. SEZCAP PIS Service & Process Certification Organic Production Certification 35% Value Addition Section Ports & Borders Library Services Mandatory Energy Labeling Scheme (SONMELS) Management System Certification Testing Services National Metrology Institute National Metrology Institute Calibration Price List Service Process Flow Chart Servic